WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Not a verdict: the two beliefs under every skill.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.560
Nadia's first presentation at her internship goes badly. She loses her place twice.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.610
That night, one sentence plays on repeat: I am just bad at presenting. It sounds like a fact. It is actually a full stop. Nothing comes after it.

4
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:24.080
A verdict about yourself leaves nothing to do next. So she crosses it out: I have not trained presenting with a method yet.

5
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:32.440
Now there is a next step: rehearse twice, out loud, with a timer.

6
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:40.860
The second belief is about energy. Nadia worries about the job market, the other interns, and what her supervisor thinks of her. None of that moves when she pushes.

7
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:48.190
Her rehearsals do. So do the questions she asks.

8
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:54.850
Energy spent inside your control compounds. Energy spent on the rest evaporates.

9
00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:01.230
So she rehearses twice with a teammate and a timer, and asks him one question: where did you lose me?

10
00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:07.100
Her second presentation is not perfect. It is clearly better. Ability turned out to be a variable.

11
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.760
Your personal audit comes next. It only works at one setting: honest. That means no self-punishment and no self-promotion.

12
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:21.160
Kind to the person, ruthless about the data. “I am bad at X” is a full stop. “I have not trained X with a method yet” is a to-do.

13
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.960
Now it is your turn. Catch one verdict in your own self-talk today, and rewrite it as a method.
